<p>A <strong>commercial property insurance claim in San Marcos</strong> carries more moving parts than a typical homeowners claim. The building may have a low-slope roof, rooftop HVAC units, and storefront glass. The policy may include coinsurance, business income, extra expense, and ordinance or law provisions, each with its own conditions. And every week the property is out of service costs money. As a San Marcos public adjuster, we represent business owners, commercial landlords, and associations, not the insurer, and help them document the physical damage and the financial loss behind it.</p>

<h2>Commercial Properties We Work With</h2>
